<article class="env-lemma" id="086W">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/086W">Lemma <span data-tag="086W">70.5.3</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X = \mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits _{i \in I} X_ i$ be the limit of a directed inverse system of algebraic spaces over $S$ with affine transition morphisms (Lemma <a href="/tag/07SF" data-tag="07SF">70.4.1</a>). If each $X_ i$ is quasi-compact and nonempty, then $|X|$ is nonempty. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose $0 \in I$. Choose an affine scheme $U_0$ and a surjective étale morphism $U_0 \to X_0$. Set $U_ i = X_ i \times _{X_0} U_0$ and $U = X \times _{X_0} U_0$. Then each $U_ i$ is a nonempty affine scheme. Hence $U = \mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits U_ i$ is nonempty (Limits, Lemma <a href="/tag/01Z2" data-tag="01Z2">32.4.3</a>) and thus $X$ is nonempty. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>